You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method Tangent(r: array<int>, x: array<int>) returns (b: bool)
    requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i <= j < x.Length ==> x[i] <= x[j] // values in x will be in ascending order or empty
    requires forall i, j :: (0 <= i < r.Length && 0 <= j < x.Length) ==> (r[i] >= 0 && x[j] >= 0)       // x and r will contain no negative values
    ensures !b ==> forall i, j :: 0 <= i< r.Length && 0 <= j < x.Length ==> r[i] != x[j]   
    ensures b ==> exists i, j :: 0 <= i< r.Length && 0 <= j < x.Length && r[i] == x[j]
{
    var tempB, tangentMissing, k, l := false, false, 0, 0;
    while k != r.Length && !tempB
        invariant 0 <= k <= r.Length
        invariant tempB ==> exists i, j :: 0 <= i < r.Length && 0 <= j < x.Length && r[i] == x[j]
        invariant !tempB ==> forall i, j :: (0 <= i<k && 0 <= j < x.Length) ==> r[i] != x[j]
        decreases r.Length - k
    {
        l:= 0;
        tangentMissing := false;
        while l != x.Length && !tangentMissing
            invariant 0 <= l <= x.Length
            invariant !tempB ==> forall i :: 0 <= i< l ==> r[k] != x[i]
            invariant tangentMissing ==> forall i :: (l <= i < x.Length) ==> r[k] != x[i]
            decreases x.Length - l, !tempB, !tangentMissing
        {

            if  r[k] == x[l] {
                tempB := true;
            }
            if (r[k] < x[l]) {
                tangentMissing := true;
            }
            l := l + 1;
        }
        k := k + 1;
    }
    b := tempB;
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(10,28): Error: this invariant could not be proved to be maintained by the loop
 Related message: loop invariant violation

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 1 error

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
At initial state: r.Length = 2, r[1] = 449, x.Length = 1, x[8856] = 448. At a program state: k = 0, l = 0, tangentMissing = false, tempB = false.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

